<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Naive comparison</stron=
g>: Character code point comparison</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Case sensitivity</stron=
g>: Different languages have different case rules</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Accent sensitivity</str=
ong>: "caf=C3=A9" vs "cafe" - same meaning?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Cultural sorting</stron=
g>: German =C3=A4 sorts after z in phonebooks but with a trong dictionaries=
</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Unicode normalization</=
strong>: Same visual character, different encodings</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">=F0=9F=92=AD <strong>Think Out L=
